{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791299429,"nonce":"udK9/Ie4KHF8DUG7ZUGmUOxslSg=","title":"HIR: specialize loops once a loop-carried tag stabilizes","message":"Lua Collatz carries an int-or-float tuple through its inner loop. After the first halving the value remains float, but the optimized LLVM IR continues carrying both payloads, doing integer and float work, and testing the tag every iteration. NUC zylua is about 154ms vs LuaJIT 135ms in the current checked benchmark. This also applies to other finite-tag recurrences in dynamic frontends.\n\nExplore a bounded shared HIR transformation: guard a scalar header phi against a constant and enter a loop copy only when the constant is proved preserved on every reachable backedge after simplification. Keep the generic loop for other states and allow it to enter the specialized loop when its state changes. Preserve live values at exits and OSR state. Do not assume arithmetic kind stability without proof, alter overflow semantics, or force promotion.","files":null}]}